IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aoma-majority`
IMPORT `aoma-qa`

-- Age of Majority Act 1972 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (aoma-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and
-- every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error
-- ("it is an assumed term"). Each question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with FALSE (the
-- situation does not hold) and every later input ASSUMEd: again `does not arise for you`. For the young person (the
-- baseline's seat) the answer is also asserted equal to the baseline export's own answer on the same facts. For the
-- other role the answers are worked by hand from the text; mirror cases ask Chloe's facts from both seats.
--
-- Facts: Chloe, born 14 March 2003, turns 18 on 14 March 2021 (WA lives, c025). The commencing day is not in the
-- deposit: 1 January 1973 is the baseline's ASSUMED placeholder, used only to exercise s 4(2) and s 5(1)(b). Other
-- people are the encoder's illustrations. Expected values are written by hand from the deposited text, never copied
-- from the output.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked date` IS A DATE
ASSUME `an unasked expression` IS A `The expression`
ASSUME `an unasked place` IS A `Where the expression appears`
ASSUME `an unasked cause` IS A `The cause of the incapacity`
ASSUME `an unasked cause of theirs` IS A `What the young person's incapacity is due to`

`as the young person` MEANS `I am the young person, asking about my own age`
`as the other person` MEANS `I am a parent, guardian, trustee or other person dealing with a young person`

`the placeholder commencing day` MEANS Date 1 1 1973
`Chloe's birthday` MEANS Date 14 3 2003

§§ `For the young person`

-- When, in law, do I reach a given age (s 4)? Chloe: 18 at the very start of 14 March 2021.
#ASSERT `When in law do I reach an age` `as the young person` `Chloe's birthday` 18 `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `the answer is` (`at the very start of` (Date 14 3 2021))
#ASSERT `When in law do I reach an age` `as the young person` (Date 29 2 2004) 18 `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `the answer is` `not fixed by the Act: I was born on 29 February and that year has no 29 February`
#ASSERT `When in law do I reach an age` `as the young person` (Date 1 6 1950) 18 `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `the answer is` `not fixed by s 4: the anniversary fell before the commencing day`
-- ... the baseline export's answer, on the same facts.
#ASSERT `When in law do I reach an age` `as the young person` `Chloe's birthday` 18 `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `the answer is` (`When do I reach this age` `Chloe's birthday` 18 `the placeholder commencing day`)
#ASSERT `When in law do I reach an age` `as the young person` (Date 29 2 2000) 20 `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `the answer is` (`When do I reach this age` (Date 29 2 2000) 20 `the placeholder commencing day`)
#ASSERT `When in law do I reach an age` `as the young person` (Date 1 6 1950) 18 `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `the answer is` (`When do I reach this age` (Date 1 6 1950) 18 `the placeholder commencing day`)
-- ... and not for the other role, nothing read.
#ASSERT `When in law do I reach an age` `as the other person` `an unasked date` `an unasked number` `an unasked date` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- When do I come of full age and full capacity (s 5(1))? Chloe: on attaining 18, at the very start of 14 March 2021.
#ASSERT `When do I come of full age and full capacity` `as the young person` `Chloe's birthday` `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `the answer is` (`on attaining 18, at the very start of` (Date 14 3 2021))
-- 19 on the commencing day: full age on that day (s 5(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `When do I come of full age and full capacity` `as the young person` (Date 1 6 1953) `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `the answer is` (`on the commencing day` (Date 1 1 1973))
#ASSERT `When do I come of full age and full capacity` `as the young person` (Date 1 1 1952) `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `the answer is` `not decided by this Act: I was 21 or over on the commencing day`
#ASSERT `When do I come of full age and full capacity` `as the young person` (Date 29 2 2004) `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `the answer is` `not decided by this Act: I was born on 29 February and my 18th year has no 29 February`
#ASSERT `When do I come of full age and full capacity` `as the young person` `Chloe's birthday` `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `the answer is` (`When do I come of full age` `Chloe's birthday` `the placeholder commencing day`)
#ASSERT `When do I come of full age and full capacity` `as the young person` (Date 1 6 1953) `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `the answer is` (`When do I come of full age` (Date 1 6 1953) `the placeholder commencing day`)
#ASSERT `When do I come of full age and full capacity` `as the other person` `an unasked date` `an unasked date` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- Am I an adult in law on a given day (s 5(1))? Chloe on 13 March 2021: not yet; on 14 March 2021: yes.
#ASSERT `Am I an adult in law on the day I ask about` `as the young person` `Chloe's birthday` (Date 13 3 2021) `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `the answer is` `not yet: I am not of full age on that day`
#ASSERT `Am I an adult in law on the day I ask about` `as the young person` `Chloe's birthday` (Date 14 3 2021) `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `the answer is` `yes: of full age and full capacity under s 5(1)(a)`
#ASSERT `Am I an adult in law on the day I ask about` `as the young person` (Date 1 6 1953) (Date 1 1 1973) `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `the answer is` `yes: of full age and full capacity under s 5(1)(b)`
#ASSERT `Am I an adult in law on the day I ask about` `as the young person` `Chloe's birthday` (Date 13 3 2021) `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `the answer is` (`Am I an adult in law on this day` `Chloe's birthday` (Date 13 3 2021) `the placeholder commencing day`)
#ASSERT `Am I an adult in law on the day I ask about` `as the young person` `Chloe's birthday` (Date 14 3 2021) `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `the answer is` (`Am I an adult in law on this day` `Chloe's birthday` (Date 14 3 2021) `the placeholder commencing day`)
#ASSERT `Am I an adult in law on the day I ask about` `as the other person` `an unasked date` `an unasked date` `an unasked date` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- Does coming of full age remove this incapacity of mine (s 5(4))? Only incapacity due to age.
#ASSERT `Does my coming of full age remove this incapacity of mine` `as the young person` TRUE `my age` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does my coming of full age remove this incapacity of mine` `as the young person` TRUE `my age` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does my coming of full age remove this incapacity of mine` `as the young person` TRUE `insanity` TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does my coming of full age remove this incapacity of mine` `as the young person` TRUE `another factor distinct from age` TRUE EQUALS no
-- ... the baseline export's answer (TRUE is yes, FALSE is no).
#ASSERT `Does my coming of full age remove this incapacity of mine` `as the young person` TRUE `my age` TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Does turning 18 remove this incapacity` `my age` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Does my coming of full age remove this incapacity of mine` `as the young person` TRUE `mental infirmity` TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Does turning 18 remove this incapacity` `mental infirmity` TRUE)
-- ... the situation does not hold: no incapacity to ask about, nothing else read.
#ASSERT `Does my coming of full age remove this incapacity of mine` `as the young person` FALSE `an unasked cause` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Does my coming of full age remove this incapacity of mine` `as the other person` `an unasked fact` `an unasked cause` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a parent, guardian, trustee or other person dealing with a young person`

-- When, in law, does the young person reach a given age (s 4)? Chloe's parent: 18 from the very start of 14 March 2021;
-- a trust that gives her capital "at 25 years": from the very start of 14 March 2028 (an age in years, s 5(3), but s 4
-- still fixes the moment).
#ASSERT `When in law does the young person reach an age` `as the other person` `Chloe's birthday` 18 `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `from the very start of` (Date 14 3 2021)
#ASSERT `When in law does the young person reach an age` `as the other person` `Chloe's birthday` 25 `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `from the very start of` (Date 14 3 2028)
#ASSERT `When in law does the young person reach an age` `as the other person` (Date 29 2 2004) 18 `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `not fixed by the Act: the young person was born on 29 February and that year has no 29 February`
#ASSERT `When in law does the young person reach an age` `as the other person` (Date 1 6 1950) 18 `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `not fixed by s 4: the anniversary fell before the commencing day`
#ASSERT `When in law does the young person reach an age` `as the young person` `an unasked date` `an unasked number` `an unasked date` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- When does the young person come of full age and full capacity (s 5(1))?
#ASSERT `When does the young person come of full age and full capacity` `as the other person` `Chloe's birthday` `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `on turning 18, from the very start of` (Date 14 3 2021)
#ASSERT `When does the young person come of full age and full capacity` `as the other person` (Date 1 6 1953) `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `on the commencing day, which was` (Date 1 1 1973)
#ASSERT `When does the young person come of full age and full capacity` `as the other person` (Date 1 1 1952) `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `not decided by this Act: the person was 21 or over on the commencing day`
#ASSERT `When does the young person come of full age and full capacity` `as the other person` (Date 29 2 2004) `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `not decided by this Act: the young person was born on 29 February and their 18th year has no 29 February`
#ASSERT `When does the young person come of full age and full capacity` `as the young person` `an unasked date` `an unasked date` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- Is the young person an adult in law on a given day (s 5(1))? A seller contracting with Chloe on 13 March 2021: not
-- yet; on 14 March 2021: yes.
#ASSERT `Is the young person an adult in law on the day I ask about` `as the other person` `Chloe's birthday` (Date 13 3 2021) `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `not yet: the young person is not of full age on that day`
#ASSERT `Is the young person an adult in law on the day I ask about` `as the other person` `Chloe's birthday` (Date 14 3 2021) `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `yes: of full age and full capacity under s 5(1)(a)`
#ASSERT `Is the young person an adult in law on the day I ask about` `as the other person` (Date 1 6 1953) (Date 1 1 1973) `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `yes: of full age and full capacity under s 5(1)(b)`
#ASSERT `Is the young person an adult in law on the day I ask about` `as the other person` (Date 1 6 1950) (Date 20 10 2026) `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `not decided by this Act: the person was 21 or over on the commencing day`
#ASSERT `Is the young person an adult in law on the day I ask about` `as the other person` (Date 29 2 2004) (Date 1 3 2022) `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `not decided by this Act: the young person was born on 29 February and their 18th year has no 29 February`
#ASSERT `Is the young person an adult in law on the day I ask about` `as the young person` `an unasked date` `an unasked date` `an unasked date` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- Does the young person's coming of full age remove this incapacity of theirs (s 5(4))?
#ASSERT `Does the young person's coming of full age remove this incapacity of theirs` `as the other person` TRUE `their age` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does the young person's coming of full age remove this incapacity of theirs` `as the other person` TRUE `their age` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does the young person's coming of full age remove this incapacity of theirs` `as the other person` TRUE `insanity` TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does the young person's coming of full age remove this incapacity of theirs` `as the other person` TRUE `mental infirmity` TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does the young person's coming of full age remove this incapacity of theirs` `as the other person` TRUE `another factor distinct from age` TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does the young person's coming of full age remove this incapacity of theirs` `as the other person` FALSE `an unasked cause of theirs` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Does the young person's coming of full age remove this incapacity of theirs` `as the young person` `an unasked fact` `an unasked cause of theirs` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

§§ `Mirror cases: Chloe's facts from both seats`

#ASSERT (`When do I come of full age and full capacity` `as the young person` `Chloe's birthday` `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `the answer is` (`on attaining 18, at the very start of` (Date 14 3 2021))) AND (`When does the young person come of full age and full capacity` `as the other person` `Chloe's birthday` `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `on turning 18, from the very start of` (Date 14 3 2021))
#ASSERT (`Am I an adult in law on the day I ask about` `as the young person` `Chloe's birthday` (Date 13 3 2021) `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `the answer is` `not yet: I am not of full age on that day`) AND (`Is the young person an adult in law on the day I ask about` `as the other person` `Chloe's birthday` (Date 13 3 2021) `the placeholder commencing day` EQUALS `not yet: the young person is not of full age on that day`)

§§ `For everyone: a word like "minor" or "adult"`

-- A WA enactment's "minor": the line of 18, for either role.
#ASSERT `How is a word like minor or adult read in this law or document` `as the young person` TRUE `minor` `a WA enactment` FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `with 18 as the line: full age and full capacity as in s 5(1)`
#ASSERT `How is a word like minor or adult read in this law or document` `as the other person` TRUE `minor` `a WA enactment` FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `with 18 as the line: full age and full capacity as in s 5(1)`
-- A trustee reading "until the beneficiary attains majority" in a trust deed made in 2010: the line of 18.
#ASSERT `How is a word like minor or adult read in this law or document` `as the other person` TRUE `majority` `a written instrument made on or after the commencing day` FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `with 18 as the line: full age and full capacity as in s 5(1)`
-- An employer reading "adult" in an industrial award: not affected (s 5(7)).
#ASSERT `How is a word like minor or adult read in this law or document` `as the other person` TRUE `adult` `an industrial award, order, determination or agreement` FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `not affected: employment and industrial instruments are excluded (s 5(7))`
-- "21 years of age" in a will: not affected (s 5(3)).
#ASSERT `How is a word like minor or adult read in this law or document` `as the other person` TRUE `an age expressed in years` `a written instrument made on or after the commencing day` FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `not affected: the age in years stands as written (s 5(3))`
-- A will of 1970 confirmed by a codicil of 1980: not affected (s 5(5)).
#ASSERT `How is a word like minor or adult read in this law or document` `as the young person` TRUE `infant` `a will made before the commencing day, confirmed by a codicil on or after it` FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `not affected: a will made before the commencing day is not remade by a later codicil (s 5(2)(b), (5))`
-- ... the baseline export's answer, for the young person.
#ASSERT `How is a word like minor or adult read in this law or document` `as the young person` TRUE `infant` `a written instrument made on or after the commencing day` TRUE EQUALS `the answer is` (`How is this expression read` `infant` `a written instrument made on or after the commencing day` TRUE)
#ASSERT `How is a word like minor or adult read in this law or document` `as the young person` TRUE `minor` `a Commonwealth law, another State's law, or a document under one` FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` (`How is this expression read` `minor` `a Commonwealth law, another State's law, or a document under one` FALSE)
-- ... the situation does not hold, for each role: nothing else read.
#ASSERT `How is a word like minor or adult read in this law or document` `as the young person` FALSE `an unasked expression` `an unasked place` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `How is a word like minor or adult read in this law or document` `as the other person` FALSE `an unasked expression` `an unasked place` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
